MoleculeStudio combines a Win32 editor, Python chemistry backend, Java
chemistry tools and an embedded Node.js/DeepSeek Harness runtime. Key
dependencies include RDKit 2024.9.6 (BSD), OPSIN 2.9.0 (MIT), JNA InChI
1.3.1 (LGPL), InChI 1.07.2 (MIT), CPython, Eclipse Temurin, LibreOffice Kit,
sharp/libvips, OpenCV and its separate FFmpeg plugin. Read the component
license files for exact versions, terms and original attribution.

The editor is compiled using MinGW GCC. GCC runtime libraries retain GPLv3
with the GCC Runtime Library Exception 3.1. That exception permits eligible
independent modules to be distributed under the project's chosen terms.
Microsoft runtime DLLs remain proprietary redistributables under their own
terms; they are not covered by Apache-2.0.

